{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6718920127","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1217#issuecomment-6718920127","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1217","id":6718920127,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkHqVvw","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?u=4a54630ef210e4f76a452eea65cda1b56370734c&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T07:48:49Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T07:48:49Z","author_association":"MEMBER","body":"Independent residual triage of W06 successor `82dce85aea7810941dfdf0bde7480bcdaa0c5826` confirms three bounded follow-ups from the sealed W09 review. All 188 cases/103 selected payloads were covered by that review; its 12 original finding groups remain resolved in their exact original scopes. This comment does not reopen them or clear any source/role/export hold.\n\n**W06-S1217-NEW-001 — seven additional stock carrier claims.** I read all seven complete selected payloads and their cited recipes. None identifies water as the carrier of that particular stock. Remove the unsupported Water entry, revise current inference notes and append truthful correction history. Retain printed solutes/strengths and UNKNOWN closure; changing only the method to CURATED_INTERPRETATION would not supply the missing evidence.\n\n| Proposal | Source scope | Exact prior payload SHA256 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `A-P-DSMZ29-CARBONATE-1M` | DSMZ29 names filter-sterilised 1 M Na2CO3 for adjusting the receiving medium to pH 6.8–7.1; DSMZ40 inherits 29 with added NaCl. [source1](https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium29.pdf), [source2](https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium40.pdf) | `c739d5e2a0901ffa8766b47220bcf1baaf29deb05a1f52f10f0301ab6f193968` |\n| `A-P-ATCC1257-CARBONATE-4PCT` | ATCC1257 lists freshly prepared filter-sterilised 4% Na2CO3, 10 ml added to the receiving medium. [source1](https://www.atcc.org/~/media/AE1BC225B681490BA78D21448457E756.ashx) | `42bb0651b003a22ab9a2a2ca754f72dd3f6cc0cec5dc1fe4f46a9e3c80701cad` |\n| `A-P-JCM1344-YEAST-1PCT` | JCM1344 adds 1 ml of separately autoclaved 1% yeast extract solution after cooling the basal medium. [source1](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=1344) | `66cce4c6df6a38d3241527db9da2a9a12061b8cfb340cb1f626d82d93bc746a3` |\n| `A-P-TOGO2665-KOH-STOCK` | TOGO M2665 explicitly names KOH solusion and classifies it as potassium hydroxide solution. ATCC1775 adds KOH during NTA dissolution/pH adjustment without stating the KOH reagent's supplied form or strength. [source1](https://www.atcc.org/~/media/385F0331DBAE42A3B87040A1D040AC39.ashx), [source2](https://togomedium.org/sparqlist/api/gmdb_medium_by_gmid?gm_id=M2665) | `c297576c743abbef6933e02c9b7081631510a4561d00684b1185fb5c302e0cd6` |\n| `B-P-DSMZ1033-ferric-stock` | DSMZ1033 lists 10 ml of a 0.17 mM FeCl3·6H2O stock. [source1](https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium1033.pdf) | `5f320423784377266082ee69866d36bd543d76d255f43dfbd4b876f6f09a1299` |\n| `B-P-DSMZ135-339a-carbonate5` | Both DSMZ135 and 339a specify sterile/anoxic 5% w/v Na2CO3 stock under 80% N2 / 20% CO2. [source1](https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium339a.pdf), [source2](https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium135.pdf) | `fffd3b28254ce6f5ce4b13fedd34232627385da7f09a51fe4fc6851fda2c9837` |\n| `B-P-ATCC1612-CARBONATE5` | ATCC1612 uses sterile anaerobic 5% Na2CO3, 0.25 ml per 10 ml medium, to adjust the medium to pH 8.2. [source1](https://www.atcc.org/~/media/BFCCC10871CB40E8A84CDDC2504F7A2E.ashx) | `f19b8aff1cc059931a95681949a1abd4d1a7a30dec36a360b1fa6b5ddde6c73e` |\n\nBasal/other-stock water cannot transfer into these preparations. For KOH, TOGO's Solution classification and the receiving NTA mixture's water do not identify the reagent solvent. For ATCC1257, the same page explicitly uses ethanol/water for other supplements. Filtration, autoclaving, anaerobic handling and w/v alone do not establish carrier identity. Preserve receiving doses/pH separately from stock composition, and do not add preparation gases as material parts. The two ferric/DSMZ135–339a evidence notes that call water a preparation input need correction too. This is not blanket removal of stock water: the separately retained MediaDive1566 source explicitly says 10% in H2O and remains a positive, version-specific control.\n\n**W06-S1217-NEW-002 — apple pectin, case 82.** [TOGO M2313](https://togomedium.org/sparqlist/api/gmdb_medium_by_gmid?gm_id=M2313) explicitly distinguishes apple pectin from citrus-peel pectin as alternative 0.2% carbon materials; its percentage basis is unstated. The apple-material boundary is known even though supplier, grade, esterification/distribution and preparation remain unknown. Complete the duplicate-safe apple-qualified material or occurrence/supplied-form assessment under §3 rather than requiring procurement details before any bounded representation. The captured ChEBI:17309 Apple-pectin entries are **related**, not exact, synonyms; do not flatten them into exact generic identity or copy generic CAS/approval onto a new material. Preserve the one-of alternatives, no simultaneous components or inferred role approval. This is related to #1201's completion mechanism and retains the prior 007 correction.\n\n**W06-S1217-NEW-003 — YNB, case 161.** [J240](https://mediadive.dsmz.de/rest/medium/J240) already identifies BD-Difco and 1 g for compound 1507. Revise only the missing-fact partition: J240's exact variant/catalog/lot and amino-acid/ammonium-sulfate inclusion remain unresolved; [DSMZ1682](https://mediadive.dsmz.de/rest/medium/1682) and [DSMZ1837](https://mediadive.dsmz.de/rest/medium/1837) each give 6.7 g without that manufacturer qualifier. Preserve the corrected quantities and no-generic-merge outcome; original 011 stays resolved.\n\nINFO004 remains informational: nominal PPG 2000, DI-water routing and a literal partial A5 representation are bounded future options, not permission to invent polymer specification, equate distilled/deionized water, or repair CuSO2·5H2O by guess. Preserve J887/MediaDive1886 provenance limits, EBIOS coordination under #1221, all 310 source occurrences and 88 downstream holds. #1226 concerns distinct mapping-evidence authorship semantics; it is not a replacement for source evidence of water.\n\nEvidence: W09 packet FINAL-MANIFEST SHA256 `09e127dff38aa4e71edac4458038ef0990304af288768777953445c5487e7218`; machine findings `4d62999c45314c1e4d74b17e301c60d3c6e4b7754d076824e127c557b471402f`. The coordinator's separate read-only triage is `C/preflight/w06-successor-residual-triage-v1/`, with exact source hashes/times, full prior values, per-field instructions and bounded duplicate/search evidence. Here C denotes the durable all-unmatched campaign root. Reuse the original 12 lineage, publish a new immutable correction and obtain independent exact-byte re-review before integration; no owner or release approval is implied.\n\n<!-- mim-fingerprints:w06-successor1217-seven-inferred-water-method,w06-successor1217-apple-pectin-bounded-representation,w06-successor1217-j240-known-supplier -->\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6718920127/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"pin":null}